Theorem TF-8: Select transfer with SCALAR exclusion + componentwise join

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Select { dst, cond, true_val, false_val }` per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-8 + Appendix A row 10
    - SCALAR is the L-9 sentinel — NOT a lattice element; `join(a, SCALAR)`
      undefined per Annex E §AIMS L-9
    - Per §3 TF-8 explicit guidance: TF-8 pre-filters SCALAR BEFORE
      invoking join (i.e. join is NEVER called on a SCALAR operand)
    - Per Annex E §AIMS L-9: SCALAR sentinel excluded from lattice
      operations; analysis SHALL exclude scalars from state map; TF-8 is
      the only join site that can receive a SCALAR operand

  Soundness property:
    Forall (true_val_state, false_val_state) in (AimsState union {SCALAR})^2.
      CASE 1 (both SCALAR): dst.state := SCALAR
      CASE 2 (exactly one SCALAR): dst inherits non-SCALAR with
        uniqueness := max(MaybeShared, non_scalar.uniqueness)
        (preserves Shared, downgrades Unique — monotone per L-6)
      CASE 3 (both non-SCALAR): dst := join(true_val.state, false_val.state)
        (standard componentwise join per L-1.proof Lift to product)
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: the one-SCALAR downgrade preserves the
    product order on the Uniqueness chain.

  Proof obligation:
    Four-part discharge:
      (a) Three-branch case analysis covering the (true_val, false_val) x
          (SCALAR, non-SCALAR) product (4 combinations collapse to 3
          equivalence classes per L-9 SCALAR sentinel handling).
      (b) CASE 2 uniqueness-downgrade enumeration: verify max(MaybeShared,
          non_scalar.uniqueness) produces the correct value for each of
          the 3 Uniqueness carrier values {Unique, MaybeShared, Shared}.
      (c) CASE 3 componentwise-join enumeration: verify the join is
          commutative (L-1) and matches componentwise per-dimension max
          per L-1.proof per-dimension argument.
      (d) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity for the CASE 2 downgrade: enumerate
          the Uniqueness chain {Unique < MaybeShared < Shared} pairs;
          verify max(MaybeShared, u1) ≤ max(MaybeShared, u2) whenever
          u1 ≤ u2.

    Part (a) — three-branch case enumeration:
      CASE 1: (SCALAR, SCALAR) -> SCALAR (L-9 sentinel propagation).
        Verified by transfer_tf8(Tagged::Scalar, Tagged::Scalar) ==
        Tagged::Scalar.
      CASE 2: (SCALAR, non_scalar) OR (non_scalar, SCALAR) -> non_scalar
        with uniqueness downgrade. Symmetric in argument order — verified
        by transfer_tf8(Scalar, ns) == transfer_tf8(ns, Scalar).
      CASE 3: (non_scalar_a, non_scalar_b) -> componentwise join.
        join is total on the carrier product (excludes SCALAR by L-9).

    Part (b) — CASE 2 uniqueness-downgrade enumeration:
      non_scalar.uniqueness = Unique:
        max(MaybeShared, Unique) = MaybeShared (downgrade)
        — Unique past-guarantee invalidated by Select branch where the
          other branch returned a scalar (not RC-tracked); the non-scalar
          value's uniqueness narrows toward MaybeShared.
      non_scalar.uniqueness = MaybeShared:
        max(MaybeShared, MaybeShared) = MaybeShared (preserve)
      non_scalar.uniqueness = Shared:
        max(MaybeShared, Shared) = Shared (preserve)
      All other dimensions inherited as-is from the non-SCALAR operand.
      6 cases enumerated (3 uniqueness x 2 argument orders).

    Part (c) — CASE 3 componentwise-join enumeration:
      Two representative non-SCALAR pairs spanning the per-dimension
      carriers:
        pair_1: (FRESH-like, CONSERVATIVE-leaning) — Access transition
          Owned -> Owned (idempotent), Consumption Linear -> Affine
          (downward), Cardinality Once -> Many (downward), Uniqueness
          Unique -> MaybeShared (downward), Locality BlockLocal ->
          FunctionLocal (downward), Shape ReusableStruct -> ReusableStruct
          (preserved), Effect 0b001 -> 0b010 (componentwise OR).
        pair_2: (CONSERVATIVE-like with HeapEscaping, CONSERVATIVE-like
          with Shared) — verifies Uniqueness MaybeShared -> Shared
          (downward) + Effect 0b100 -> 0b001 (componentwise OR).
      For each pair (a, b):
        - L-1 commutativity check: transfer_tf8(a, b) == transfer_tf8(b, a).
        - Componentwise max check: result = (dim_max(ACCESS, a, b),
          dim_max(CONSUMPTION, a, b), dim_max(CARDINALITY, a, b),
          dim_max(UNIQUENESS, a, b), dim_max(LOCALITY, a, b),
          (if shapes equal: shape; else: NonReusable),
          (effect_a OR effect_b)).
      2 pairs enumerated; covers the full per-dimension product order
      lift per L-1.proof.

    Part (d) — L-6 layer (b) monotonicity for CASE 2 downgrade:
      Uniqueness chain {Unique < MaybeShared < Shared} has 3 elements,
      6 ordered pairs (u1, u2) with u1 ≤ u2. For each pair:
        d1 := max(MaybeShared, u1)
        d2 := max(MaybeShared, u2)
        Verify d1 ≤ d2.
      Specifically:
        (Unique, Unique) -> (MaybeShared, MaybeShared) — MaybeShared ≤ MaybeShared OK
        (Unique, MaybeShared) -> (MaybeShared, MaybeShared) — ≤ OK
        (Unique, Shared) -> (MaybeShared, Shared) — MaybeShared ≤ Shared OK
        (MaybeShared, MaybeShared) -> (MaybeShared, MaybeShared) — ≤ OK
        (MaybeShared, Shared) -> (MaybeShared, Shared) — ≤ OK
        (Shared, Shared) -> (Shared, Shared) — ≤ OK
      All 6 pairs satisfy monotonicity. Per L-6.proof per-dimension
      monotonicity argument: max on a totally-ordered carrier is monotone
      (proved generally there); TF-8 downgrade is a specific instance.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-rule discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf8_select_scalar_exclusion — Part (d)
        Uniqueness-chain enumeration)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — three-branch case enumeration (CASE 1 / 2 / 3)
        + 6-pair Uniqueness-downgrade enumeration + 2-pair componentwise-
        join enumeration per
        section_04::verify_tf8_select_scalar_exclusion)
      lattice (SECONDARY — gracefully accepts; L-9 SCALAR pre-filter +
        L-1 commutativity discharged at §02 lattice engine)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-8 is a join site,
        not a refine() site)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-8 via three-branch case enumeration (both-SCALAR / one-SCALAR / both-non-SCALAR) + L-9 SCALAR pre-filter call-site enumeration + Uniqueness-chain monotone-downgrade discharge
